      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, twice the maximum daily dose. I know of no indication that supports it, and the added risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events outweighs any benefit. Taking responsibility for the order doesn't change that risk to the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum right away.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or a lower dose.\n- **Help with the underlying goal.** If this patient needs more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than ibuprofen can give, I can enter an adjunct or alternative. Tell me what you're treating.\n- **Consult pharmacy or the attending.** If you think there's an unusual reason for this dose, they can review it and enter it through the appropriate channel.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter the order."
      }
